{
  "case_id": "2021-21-499",
  "document_hash": "5b39af57a191e4ffa6dc532fdfadf86f90a84f196e9c2331d6c16f91afd0a215",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Tekoh",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b39af57a191e4ffa6dc532fdfadf86f90a84f196e9c2331d6c16f91afd0a215",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b39af57a191-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Tekoh argues that a violation of Miranda constitutes a violation of the Fifth Amendment right against compelled self-incrimination."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b39af57a191e4ffa6dc532fdfadf86f90a84f196e9c2331d6c16f91afd0a215",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b39af57a191-0000-0003",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We hold that it does not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ninth Circuit",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b39af57a191e4ffa6dc532fdfadf86f90a84f196e9c2331d6c16f91afd0a215",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b39af57a191-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Ninth Circuit held\u2014and Tekoh now argues, Brief for Respondent 20\u2014that a violation of Miranda constitutes a violation of the Fifth Amendment right against compelled self-incrimination, but that is wrong."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b39af57a191e4ffa6dc532fdfadf86f90a84f196e9c2331d6c16f91afd0a215",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b39af57a191-0001-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Allowing \u00a7 1983 suits based on Miranda claims could also present many procedural issues, such as whether a federal court considering a \u00a7 1983 claim would owe any deference to a trial court's factual fndings; whether forfeiture and plain error rules carry over from the criminal trial; whether harmless-error rules apply; and whether civil damages are available in instances where the unwarned statement had no impact on the outcome of the criminal case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b39af57a191e4ffa6dc532fdfadf86f90a84f196e9c2331d6c16f91afd0a215",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b39af57a191-0002-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "tells us in no uncertain terms that Miranda is a \u201cconstitutional rule.\u201d 530 U. S. 428, 444 (2000). And that rule grants a corresponding right: If police fail to provide the Miranda warnings to a suspect before interrogating him, then he is generally entitled to have any resulting confession excluded from his trial."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b39af57a191e4ffa6dc532fdfadf86f90a84f196e9c2331d6c16f91afd0a215",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b39af57a191-0002-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Dickerson tells us again and again that Miranda is a \u201cconstitutional rule.\u201d 530 U. S., at 444."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b39af57a191e4ffa6dc532fdfadf86f90a84f196e9c2331d6c16f91afd0a215",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b39af57a191-0002-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Miranda's constitutional rule gives suspects a correlative \u201cright[ ].\u201d \u00a7 1983."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b39af57a191e4ffa6dc532fdfadf86f90a84f196e9c2331d6c16f91afd0a215",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b39af57a191-0002-0003",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The majority basically agrees with everything I've just explained. It concurs that, per Dickerson , Miranda \u201cadopted a `constitutional rule.' \u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b39af57a191e4ffa6dc532fdfadf86f90a84f196e9c2331d6c16f91afd0a215",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b39af57a191-0002-0004",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Compare the majority's holding today to a prior decision, in which the Court \u201crejected [an] attempt[ ] to limit the types of constitutional rights that are encompassed within\u201d \u00a7 1983."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5b39af57a191e4ffa6dc532fdfadf86f90a84f196e9c2331d6c16f91afd0a215",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5b39af57a191-0002-0005",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The point of \u00a7 1983 is to provide such redress\u2014because a remedy \u201cis a vital component of any scheme for vindicating cherished constitutional guarantees.\u201d"
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
